---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy, Advertising & Cookie Disclosure"
  description="Privacy policy, Google AdSense DART cookie disclosure, and affiliate link transparency for The Silicon Ledger."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-4xl border-2 border-[#141413] bg-[#FCFBF8] p-8 shadow-[6px_6px_0px_#141413]">
    <div class="mb-3 font-mono text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-[#D9381E]">
      Legal &amp; Ad Network Compliance
    </div>
    <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl font-extrabold text-[#141413]">
      Privacy Policy &amp; Advertising Disclosure
    </h1>

    <div class="prose prose-stone mt-6 max-w-none prose-headings:font-serif prose-headings:font-bold prose-p:text-[#141413]">
      <p><strong>Effective Date:</strong> November 13, 2026</p>

      <h2>1. Programmatic Advertising &amp; Google AdSense Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on a user's prior visits to this website or other websites on the internet. Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads to our readers based on their visit to The Silicon Ledger and/or other sites on the Internet.
      </p>
      <p>
        Users may opt out of personalized advertising by visiting <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Ads Settings</a> or <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">www.aboutads.info</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Affiliate Commerce Disclosure</h2>
      <p>
        The Silicon Ledger participates in retail affiliate programs, including the Amazon Services LLC Associates Program. As an Amazon Associate, we earn from qualifying purchases made through tagged links in our verdict boxes and price comparison tables. Editorial scores are never influenced by affiliate partnerships.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Reader Polls &amp; Local Storage</h2>
      <p>
        Our interactive hardware upgrade calculators and reader flashpolls store your selected preference locally in your browser's <code>localStorage</code> solely to display your vote state. We do not sell personal data to third parties.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
